{
 "sub_strand": "MATH.G7.MEASUR.TIME_DISTANCE_AND_SPEED",
 "title": "Time, Distance and Speed",
 "status": "draft: written 17 Nov 2026 offline for the Grade 7 pilot; not yet checked by a Kenyan maths teacher; not loaded by the live tutor",
 "sources": [],
 "notes": "Official outcomes a to f are tested; g (reflect on the use of time, distance and speed) is 'kicd_read' and an attitude. Speed is distance divided by time. The 24-hour clock is used for timetables. Conversion between km/h and m/s uses 3.6. Minutes are never written as hundredths of an hour.",
